  "description": "The same house battery bank as `house`, seen by a second source: the WattCycle 314Ah BMS read over BLE by driver-wattcycle (the Venus SmartShunt is `house`). Two sources for one bank: the Primary battery setting picks which instance is the headline. Synthetic, not captured: values sit slightly off the shunt's (a BMS and a shunt never agree exactly) and follow the same load steps as `house`. No time-to-go: a BMS does not report it. Carries the BMS's per-cell data (4 cells, 4 probes): cell voltages sag under the load steps, one cell balances at the end of the loop, a brief `cell_undervoltage` protection (danger) shows at the heaviest load, and later a brief `cell_imbalance` protection (advisory) shows while a cell balances; the two windows never overlap, so the dashboard's amber and danger BMS alerts are seen one after the other (values synthetic).",
